John Snow, Map 1 (1855)
-----------------------

Datasets: deaths (one point per bar Snow drew, 580) and pumps (the 13
pumps on his map). The workflow's results are made from these two.

The work: John Snow (1813-1858), On the mode of communication of
cholera, second edition, much enlarged, London: John Churchill, 1855.
Map 1, "Scale 30 inches to a mile", shows the deaths from cholera in and
around Broad Street, Golden Square, in late August and early September
1854, a black bar for each death at its house, and the street pumps.
Snow died in 1858; the work is in the public domain everywhere.

Licence: recorded as CC-PDM-1.0, the Public Domain Mark, as the
Wellcome Collection marks its scan.
https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/mark/1.0/

Credit: After John Snow, 1855; scan: Wellcome Collection, Public Domain
Mark.

